== 8. What this settles ========================================
  If the max rule returns STOP for RASSF9, then no choice of sequencing
  profile could have produced a testable correlation, and the arbitrary
  duplicate handling in script 42 is no longer a caveat worth stating.

  If the max rule returns MARGINAL or PROCEED, script 42's verdict was an
  artefact of keeping the first profile. In that case do NOT defend it --
  download OmicsProfiles.csv, use IsDefaultEntryForModel, and redo the
  gate properly before anything goes to Gustavo.

  WHAT THIS CANNOT SAY: nothing here addresses whether the RASSF9
  promoter is methylated in these lines. Low expression with uniform
  hypermethylation and low expression with an unmethylated promoter look
  identical in this script and mean opposite things. That is step 2.
